dict(slug="crema-pastelera-y-sus-derivadas", cat="pasteleria", fecha="2026-10-29",
 img="https://images.pexels.com/photos/33775651/pexels-photo-33775651/free-photo-of-whisk-in-action-with-creamy-custard.jpeg", foto="Pexels",
 es=dict(
  titulo="Crema pastelera y sus derivadas: diplomata, mousseline, chiboust y frangipane",
  bajada="La crema madre de la pastelería: la receta de la escuela, cómo no cortarla y las cuatro cremas que salen de ella.",
  cuerpo=[
   ("p","La crema pastelera es la crema con más usos en pastelería: rellena tartas, facturas, éclairs y profiteroles, y también se hornea. Se la considera una <strong>crema madre</strong>, porque de ella salen muchas otras."),
   ("h2","Ingredientes"),
   ("tabla",["Ingrediente","Cantidad"],[
     ["Leche","500 cc"],
     ["Yemas","6"],
     ["Azúcar","120 g"],
     ["Almidón de maíz","40 g"],
     ["Manteca fría y esencia de vainilla","Al final, a gusto"],
   ]),
   ("h2","Paso a paso"),
   ("ol",["Llevá a hervor la leche con la mitad del azúcar.","En un bowl mezclá el resto del azúcar con el almidón y sumá las yemas.","Volcá la leche caliente sobre las yemas, revolviendo bien, y llevá todo de nuevo al fuego.","Mové sin parar con batidor de alambre hasta que espese y rompa el hervor. Cociná 2 minutos más sin dejar de revolver.","Fuera del fuego, agregá la manteca fría y la esencia.","Pasala a una placa, cubrila con film en contacto (pegado a la crema, para que no forme piel) y refrigerá."]),
   ("tip","Tiene que hervir: si el almidón no llega a hervor y a cocinarse un par de minutos, la crema queda con gusto a harina y se licúa al día siguiente."),
   ("dato","Es una preparación muy delicada desde lo bacteriológico: no la guardes más de tres días en la heladera."),
   ("h2","Las derivadas"),
   ("tabla",["Crema","Qué lleva","Para qué"],[
     ["Diplomata","Pastelera + crema batida + sabor","Más liviana. En la escuela, de café y chocolate para éclairs"],
     ["Mousseline","Pastelera + manteca + sabor","Firme y aterciopelada. Rellena el Paris-Brest"],
     ["Chiboust","Pastelera + merengue italiano + gelatina","La de la torta Saint Honoré"],
     ["Frangipane","Pastelera + pasta de almendras","Para tartas que van al horno"],
   ]),
   ("h2","Diplomata de café y chocolate"),
   ("p","250 g de crema pastelera, 125 g de crema de leche, 100 g de chocolate cobertura negro y 1 cucharada de café instantáneo diluido. Se funde el chocolate a baño María, se bate la crema a 3/4 con el café, se integra el chocolate a la pastelera con batidor y se unen las dos preparaciones en forma envolvente con espátula. A la manga y al frío."),
   ("h2","Mousseline de almendras"),
   ("p","250 g de crema pastelera y 250 g de manteca, más praliné y una cucharada de esencia de vainilla. Se bate la pastelera y, con la batidora andando, se suma la manteca en cubos chicos, de forma constante, hasta que quede homogénea y aterciopelada. Al final, la esencia y el praliné picado."),
   ("h2","Para personalizarla"),
   ("ul",["Parte de la leche por crema, para un resultado más cremoso.","Aromatizada con cáscara de limón o naranja, canela, anís estrellado o clavo.","Con huevos enteros en lugar de solo yemas (por ejemplo, tres huevos y tres yemas por litro).","Con más o menos espesante según el uso: más firme para facturas, más suave para rellenar."]),
   ("p","Es el relleno clásico de la <a href=\"/blog/pate-a-choux-masa-bomba\">pâte à choux</a>."),
  ]),
 en=dict(
  titulo="Pastry cream and its variations: diplomat, mousseline, chiboust and frangipane",
  bajada="The mother cream of pastry: the school recipe, how not to split it and the four creams that come from it.",
  cuerpo=[
   ("p","Pastry cream is the most versatile cream in pastry: it fills tarts, pastries, éclairs and profiteroles, and it can also be baked. It's considered a <strong>mother cream</strong>, because many others come from it."),
   ("h2","Ingredients"),
   ("tabla",["Ingredient","Amount"],[
     ["Milk","500 ml"],
     ["Egg yolks","6"],
     ["Sugar","120 g"],
     ["Cornstarch","40 g"],
     ["Cold butter and vanilla extract","At the end, to taste"],
   ]),
   ("h2","Step by step"),
   ("ol",["Bring the milk to a boil with half the sugar.","In a bowl, mix the rest of the sugar with the cornstarch and add the yolks.","Pour the hot milk over the yolks, stirring well, and return everything to the heat.","Whisk constantly until it thickens and comes to a boil. Cook 2 more minutes, still whisking.","Off the heat, add the cold butter and the vanilla.","Spread it on a tray, cover with plastic wrap touching the surface (so no skin forms) and chill."]),
   ("tip","It has to boil: if the starch doesn't boil and cook for a couple of minutes, the cream tastes floury and turns runny the next day."),
   ("dato","It's very sensitive bacteriologically: don't keep it more than three days in the fridge."),
   ("h2","The variations"),
   ("tabla",["Cream","What goes in","What for"],[
     ["Diplomat","Pastry cream + whipped cream + flavor","Lighter. At school, coffee and chocolate for éclairs"],
     ["Mousseline","Pastry cream + butter + flavor","Firm and velvety. Fills the Paris-Brest"],
     ["Chiboust","Pastry cream + Italian meringue + gelatin","The one in the Saint Honoré cake"],
     ["Frangipane","Pastry cream + almond paste","For tarts that go in the oven"],
   ]),
   ("h2","Coffee and chocolate diplomat cream"),
   ("p","250 g pastry cream, 125 g heavy cream, 100 g dark couverture chocolate and 1 tablespoon dissolved instant coffee. Melt the chocolate over a bain-marie, whip the cream to 3/4 with the coffee, whisk the chocolate into the pastry cream, then fold the two together with a spatula. Into a piping bag and into the fridge."),
   ("h2","Almond mousseline"),
   ("p","250 g pastry cream and 250 g butter, plus praline and a tablespoon of vanilla. Beat the pastry cream and, with the mixer running, add the butter in small cubes, steadily, until smooth and velvety. Finish with the vanilla and chopped praline."),
   ("h2","Make it your own"),
   ("ul",["Swap some of the milk for cream for a richer result.","Flavor it with lemon or orange zest, cinnamon, star anise or clove.","Use whole eggs instead of just yolks (for example, three eggs and three yolks per liter).","Use more or less thickener depending on the use: firmer for baked pastries, softer for fillings."]),
   ("p","It's the classic filling for <a href=\"/blog/pate-a-choux-masa-bomba\">pâte à choux</a>."),
  ])),
